    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A particle is projected from the origin at $60^\\circ$ with speed $v$. It reaches the ground after $5.1$ s. Find $v$ to 2 d.p. Use $g=9.8\\text{ m s}^{-2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$v=28.86\\text{ m s}^{-1}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=\\frac{v}{2}t\\\\y(t)&=-4.9t^2+\\frac{v\\sqrt{3}}{2}t\\end{aligned}$$\nAt $t=5.1$, $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}0&=-4.9(5.1)^2+\\frac{v\\sqrt{3}}{2}(5.1)\\\\v&=\\frac{2(4.9)(5.1)}{\\sqrt{3}}\\\\v&\\approx28.86\\text{ m s}^{-1}\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 39
  },
